        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Notes for today"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Begin with a slow breath. This page is a "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "italic"
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--tt-color-highlight-yellow)"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "private place"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to hold prayer, questions, and the verses that stay with you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When you want fuller context, open "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "attrs": {
                "href": "https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+3&version=WEB",
                "target": "_blank",
                "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
                "class": null
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "John 3 in the World English Bible"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in another tab."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "biblePassage",
      "attrs": {
        "usfm": "JHN.3.16-17",
        "reference": "John 3:16-17",
        "versionId": 0,
        "versionTitle": "World English Bible"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For God so loved the world, that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life. For God didn't send his Son into the world to judge the world, but that the world might be saved through him."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "John 3:16-17 (World English Bible). Scripture courtesy of YouVersion."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let that promise land where you need it most. Underline what stands out, add your own "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--tt-color-highlight-blue)"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "questions and prayers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in the lines below."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Lamentations 3:22-23 — It is because of Yahweh's loving kindnesses that we are not consumed, because his mercies don't fail. They are new every morning. Great is your faithfulness."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": null,
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Carry these words"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
            "textAlign": null
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "text": "In nothing be anxious, but in everything, by prayer and petition with thanksgiving, let your requests be made known to God. And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your thoughts in Christ Jesus."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Philippians 4:6-7 (WEB). When anxiety rises, return to the pattern: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ask"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "thank"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "trust"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " the peace that guards your mind."
        }
      ]
    },
